**New evidence**
- Buhari’s office said Nigeria prioritized the safety and human rights of stranded Nigerians and supported all diplomatic efforts to end the Russia-Ukraine war.
SOURCE_CLAIM_JSON: {"title":"Statement on Nigerian and Citizens of Other African Countries in Ukraine","publisher":"The State House, Abuja","publication_date":"2022-02-27","url":"https://statehouse.gov.ng/statement-on-nigerian-and-citizens-of-other-african-countries-in-ukraine/","claim":"While talks between Russia and Ukraine were underway, Buhari's office said the safety and human rights of stranded Nigerian and other African citizens were paramount and that Nigeria supported all diplomatic efforts to end the war.","locator":"lines 27 and 48","source_type":"official","source_confidence":"high","source_confidence_reason":"Primary presidential office statement dated to the target period and directly attributable to Buhari's administration.","final_evidence_use":"final_evidence","period_fit":"Direct 2022 target period","ruler_attribution":"Direct presidential statement; it reflects Buhari's public foreign-policy stance during the period.","contrary_evidence":["This is rhetoric and evacuation framing, not a documented ceasefire or settlement outcome."],"lenses":["2B.1","2B.4","2B.7","2B.10"]}

- Buhari approved emergency evacuation funding for Nigerians trapped by the Russia-Ukraine war.
SOURCE_CLAIM_JSON: {"title":"Buhari orders release of $8.5m to evacuate Nigerians caught up in Russia-Ukraine war","publisher":"The Guardian Nigeria","publication_date":"2022-03-02","url":"https://guardian.ng/news/buhari-orders-release-of-8-5m-to-evacuate-nigerians-caught-up-in-russia-ukraine-war/","claim":"Buhari approved $8.5 million to facilitate the immediate evacuation of at least 5,000 Nigerians fleeing the Russia-Ukraine war.","locator":"lines 92-97","source_type":"media","source_confidence":"medium_high","source_confidence_reason":"Contemporaneous local reporting quoting government officials on a specific presidential approval and evacuation plan.","final_evidence_use":"final_evidence","period_fit":"Direct 2022 target period","ruler_attribution":"Directly attributed to Buhari through the approval described by ministers.","contrary_evidence":["This shows humanitarian response, not conflict de-escalation by itself."],"lenses":["2B.4","2B.7"]}

- By July 2022, the Nigerian government said 1,625 citizens had been evacuated from Ukraine.
SOURCE_CLAIM_JSON: {"title":"FG: 1,625 Nigerians evacuated from Ukraine","publisher":"TheCable","publication_date":"2022-07-08","url":"https://www.thecable.ng/fg-1625-nigerians-evacuated-from-ukraine/","claim":"The federal government said 1,625 citizens had been evacuated from Ukraine following the Russian invasion.","locator":"lines 65-70 and 79-80","source_type":"media","source_confidence":"medium_high","source_confidence_reason":"Contemporaneous Nigerian media reporting on an official government update; useful corroboration of the evacuation effort.","final_evidence_use":"final_evidence","period_fit":"Direct 2022 target period","ruler_attribution":"This is attributable to Buhari's government and evacuation policy, though not to his personal command of the flights.","contrary_evidence":["It confirms an evacuation outcome, but not the full scale of need or operational quality."],"lenses":["2B.4","2B.10"]}

- Buhari urged more cross-border collaboration against insecurity and linked the Ukraine war to global food-security strain and Sahel instability.
SOURCE_CLAIM_JSON: {"title":"President Buhari Calls for more International Collaboration to Tackle Insecurity","publisher":"The State House, Abuja","publication_date":"2022-08-02","url":"https://statehouse.gov.ng/president-buhari-calls-for-more-international-collaboration-to-tackle-insecurity/","claim":"Buhari urged more collaboration across borders to check terrorism, banditry and insurgency, and said the war in Ukraine had undermined global food security while instability in Libya continued to fuel terrorism in the Sahel and West/Central Africa.","locator":"lines 27 and 29-31","source_type":"official","source_confidence":"high","source_confidence_reason":"Primary presidential statement, clearly dated, with direct foreign-policy and security framing.","final_evidence_use":"final_evidence","period_fit":"Direct 2022 target period","ruler_attribution":"Directly attributable to Buhari as head of state and public security spokesman.","contrary_evidence":["The claim about broader causal links is interpretive and not itself proof of policy effectiveness."],"lenses":["2B.1","2B.3","2B.7","2B.10"]}

- Buhari said arms from the Russia-Ukraine war and Libya were filtering into the Lake Chad region and called for tighter border security.
SOURCE_CLAIM_JSON: {"title":"President Buhari Calls for Tighter Security Around Borders in Lake Chad Basin with the Proliferation of Weapons from Russia-Ukraine War","publisher":"The State House, Abuja","publication_date":"2022-11-29","url":"https://statehouse.gov.ng/president-buhari-calls-for-tighter-security-around-borders-in-lake-chad-basin-with-the-proliferation-of-weapons-from-russia-ukraine-war/","claim":"Buhari said weapons from the wars in Libya and Ukraine were filtering into the Lake Chad region, heightening small-arms proliferation, and he urged border-control agencies and security services to stop the illegal flow.","locator":"lines 28-35 and 41-50","source_type":"official","source_confidence":"high","source_confidence_reason":"Primary presidential speech tied to a dated regional security summit.","final_evidence_use":"final_evidence","period_fit":"Direct 2022 target period","ruler_attribution":"Direct Buhari attribution, but the underlying causal claim is his assertion and must be checked independently.","contrary_evidence":["The causal claim is contested and should not be treated as settled fact without external corroboration."],"lenses":["2B.3","2B.6","2B.7","2B.8","2B.10"]}

- VOA fact-check found Buhari’s Lake Chad weapons claim unsubstantiated.
SOURCE_CLAIM_JSON: {"title":"Unsubstantiated: Buhari Claim That Ukraine War Feeds Arms to West Africa","publisher":"VOA","publication_date":"2022-12-05","url":"https://www.voanews.com/a/fact-check-buhari-claim-ukraine-war-feeds-arms-to-west-africa/6863147.html","claim":"VOA concluded that Buhari's assertion that weapons from the Ukraine war were entering West Africa lacked public evidence and was unsubstantiated.","locator":"lines 103-109","source_type":"media","source_confidence":"medium_high","source_confidence_reason":"Independent fact-checking outlet assessing a specific Buhari claim against available evidence.","final_evidence_use":"final_evidence","period_fit":"Direct 2022 target period","ruler_attribution":"It addresses Buhari's own statement and the evidentiary support for it.","contrary_evidence":["VOA is a fact-check, not a comprehensive arms-trafficking investigation, so it can disprove overclaiming without mapping the whole trafficking network."],"lenses":["2B.6","2B.9"]}

- Buhari framed ECOWAS as needing economic integration, political stability, social harmony, conflict management, security, democracy, and rule of law.
SOURCE_CLAIM_JSON: {"title":"The ECOWAS we Desire, and Must Have, By President Buhari","publisher":"The State House, Abuja","publication_date":"2022-08-11","url":"https://statehouse.gov.ng/the-ecowas-we-desire-and-must-have-by-president-buhari/","claim":"Buhari said West African leaders needed an ECOWAS that was economically integrated, politically stable, and socially harmonious, and that conflict management, security, democracy, and rule of law remained central regional tasks.","locator":"lines 45-55","source_type":"official","source_confidence":"high","source_confidence_reason":"Primary presidential audience statement with explicit regional peace/governance framing.","final_evidence_use":"final_evidence","period_fit":"Direct 2022 target period","ruler_attribution":"Directly Buhari's own statement as Nigeria's president and ECOWAS host state leader.","contrary_evidence":["This is a stated preference and agenda, not proof that outcomes matched the rhetoric."],"lenses":["2B.1","2B.7","2B.10"]}

- Buhari said Nigeria and ECOWAS had helped restore peace and democracy in Guinea-Bissau, including sanctions on 19 individuals obstructing the Conakry Agreement.
SOURCE_CLAIM_JSON: {"title":"President Buhari Vows the Defence of Democracy In Africa","publisher":"The State House, Abuja","publication_date":"2022-12-07","url":"https://statehouse.gov.ng/president-buhari-vows-the-defence-of-democracy-in-africa/","claim":"Buhari said Nigeria, through ECOWAS, had supported Guinea-Bissau's democratic order and imposed sanctions on 19 individuals who impeded implementation of the Conakry Agreement, helping restore peace in the country.","locator":"lines 27-35","source_type":"official","source_confidence":"high","source_confidence_reason":"Primary presidential visit statement with concrete regional action and sanction details.","final_evidence_use":"final_evidence","period_fit":"Direct 2022 target period","ruler_attribution":"Directly attributable to Buhari as the visiting head of state describing Nigeria's role.","contrary_evidence":["The source is self-presentational and does not independently verify each sanction's causal effect."],"lenses":["2B.5","2B.7","2B.10"]}

- ECOWAS convened an extraordinary summit after the Burkina Faso coup and deployed missions to talk to the military authorities.
SOURCE_CLAIM_JSON: {"title":"ECOWAS Heads of State to meet in Accra for another Extraordinary Summit on the Political Situation in Burkina Faso","publisher":"Economic Community of West African States","publication_date":"2022-02-02","url":"https://www.ecowas.int/ecowas-heads-of-state-to-meet-in-accra-for-another-extraordinary-summit-on-the-political-situation-in-burkina-faso/","claim":"ECOWAS convened an extraordinary summit after the January 24, 2022 coup in Burkina Faso and deployed a high-level mission of defence chiefs followed by a joint ministerial mission to consult the military leaders and assess the situation.","locator":"lines 96-100","source_type":"IGO","source_confidence":"high","source_confidence_reason":"Official regional-body announcement describing the summit and the response mechanism it activated.","final_evidence_use":"context","period_fit":"Direct 2022 target period","ruler_attribution":"This is regional context Buhari's Nigeria was participating in, not a personal order issued by him alone.","contrary_evidence":["The page does not by itself show Buhari's individual voting or bargaining position."],"lenses":["2B.7","2B.10"]}

- Buhari publicly backed peaceful resolution and reconciliation on the Korean peninsula and said Nigeria would continue to support peace initiatives in West Africa.
SOURCE_CLAIM_JSON: {"title":"President Buhari Calls for Lasting Peace on Korean Peninsula","publisher":"The State House, Abuja","publication_date":"2022-02-11","url":"https://statehouse.gov.ng/president-buhari-calls-for-lasting-peace-on-korean-peninsula/","claim":"Buhari said Nigeria would support efforts to bring peaceful resolution and reconciliation on the Korean peninsula, and that his administration would continue to support peace initiatives and efforts in the West African sub-region.","locator":"lines 45-49 and 63-68","source_type":"official","source_confidence":"high","source_confidence_reason":"Primary presidential video-message text, dated and directly attributable to Buhari.","final_evidence_use":"final_evidence","period_fit":"Direct 2022 target period","ruler_attribution":"Direct Buhari speech, though the Korean-peninsula part is largely rhetorical and general-purpose diplomacy.","contrary_evidence":["General peace rhetoric does not prove concrete conflict settlement by itself."],"lenses":["2B.1","2B.7","2B.10"]}

**Search and rejection summary**
I considered roughly 30 documents across State House releases, ECOWAS communiqués, UN records, TheCable, Guardian Nigeria, Reuters-syndicated items, VOA fact-checking, and several duplicate or secondary explainers.

Accepted items were kept because they added something materially distinct: evacuation orders, actual evacuation count, regional diplomacy, ECOWAS stabilization language, or a fact-check on Buhari’s Lake Chad claim.

I rejected or de-prioritized:
- Duplicate syndications of the same Ukraine, ECOWAS, or evacuation story.
- Reuters Connect image pages with no usable text beyond the caption.
- General Ukraine explainers and broad Africa-security commentary that did not add Buhari-specific conduct.
- Purely domestic security items, because Chapter 2B is about international peace, not internal repression.
- Out-of-period material from 2020, 2024, or later when it did not add a 2022-targeted point.
- Unblocked but weak pages that repeated the same claim already covered by a better primary source.

One direct Reuters page was not fetchable in this environment, so I used accessible Reuters-syndicated or alternative independent copies where needed.

**Remaining gaps**
- I did not find evidence that Buhari initiated or prolonged any cross-border war in 2022, and the local prior already points the other way with zero internationalized conflict events or fatalities.
- I did not find a strong, ruler-specific record of ceasefire negotiation success beyond ECOWAS diplomacy and evacuation/humanitarian response.
- The Lake Chad arms-flow claim remains the least secure point in the file, and VOA’s fact-check cuts against treating it as established fact.
- I did not find meaningful evidence of proxy warfare, overseas military escalation, or territorial coercion attributable to Buhari in 2022.
- More searching might slightly sharpen the ECOWAS and UN voting record, but I do not think it would materially change the chapter picture.
